### Claude / Codex CLI flag drift

**Status**: parked.

**Why parked**: `make preflight-review-tooling` invokes both CLIs with the
exact flag shape the review targets use (`codex exec --sandbox read-only
--color never --output-last-message`, `claude --print --permission-mode
plan --add-dir --output-format text`). If a future CLI release renames or
removes any of these flags, preflight will fail. The tested baselines are
codex-cli 0.130.0 and Claude Code 2.1.139.

**Triggers to pick up**:
- `make preflight-review-tooling` fails on a developer machine.
- A CLI release-note explicitly deprecates one of the flags above.

**Rough effort**: ~15 minutes per flag (update Makefile + bump baseline
version in preflight's WARN line).

